// The grasslands' own animals (V2-10 (b)), Palearctic and Nearctic: the great grazers of the
// steppe and the prairie (bison, wild horse, saiga, pronghorn), the burrowers that the plains
// are built on (prairie dogs, marmots, sousliks), their hunters (coyote, the small foxes,
// badger, ferret, polecat, eagle), the open country's birds. Values rounded from general mammal
// and ornithological references and grassland field studies; densities for good habitat.
